  "summary": "Abstract Flow regime is a major determinant of the structure and functioning of aquatic ecosystems. Under climate change, flow intermittency is becoming more prevalent in glaciated alpine catchments, but the effects of increasing dryness on",
  "tags": [],
  "content_fetched": true,
  "pdf": null,
  "cid": "6275e48faa933ee4",
