partment of \nEnvironment, Great Lakes, and Energy. https:// www. mcgi. state. \nmi. us/ envir onmen talma pper/\nOffice of Brownfields and Land Revitalization (2022) Overview of \nEPA’s brownfields program. Retrieved August 3, 2022, from \nhttps:// www. epa. gov/ brown fields/ overv iew- epas- brown fields- \nprogr am\nOrd JK, Getis A (1995) Local spatial autocorrelation statistics: distri-\nbutional issues and an application. Geogr Anal 27(4):286–306. \nhttps:// doi. org/ 10. 1111/j. 1538- 4632. 1995. tb009 12.x\nPembury Smith MQR, Ruxton GD (2020) Effective use of the McNe-\nmar test. Behav Ecol Sociobiol 74(11):133. https:// doi. org/ 10. \n1007/ s00265- 020- 02916-y\nR Core Team (2013) R: a language and environment for statistical com-\nputing. R Foundation for Statistical Computing, Vienna.  http:// \nwww.R- proje ct. org/\nRatnapradipa D, Middleton WK, Wodika AB, Brown SL, Preihs K \n(2015) What does the public know about environmental health? \nA qualitative approach to refining an environmental health aware-\nness instrument. J Environ Health 77(8):22–29\nReddy KR, Adams JA (2015) Sustainable remediation of contaminated \nsites. Momentum Press, New York, 160 p\nSchultz T, Fielding K, Newton F, Louis W (2018) The effect of images \non community engagement with sustainable stormwater manage-\nment: the role of integral disgust and sadness. J Environ Psychol \n59:26–35\nSmith JWN (2019) Debunking myths about sustainable remediation. \nRemediat J 29(2):7–15. https:// doi. org/ 10. 1002/ rem. 21587\nSolitare L, Greenberg M (2002) Is the US Environmental Protection \nAgency brownfields assessment pilot program environmentally \njust? Environ Health Perspect 110(suppl 2):249–257\nU.S. Census Bureau (2020) American community survey 2019. \nRetrieved August 3, 2021, from https:// www. census. gov/ progr \nams- surve ys/ acs\nWilson S, Zhang H, Burwell K, Samantapudi A, Dalemarre L, Jiang C \net al (2013) Leaking underground storage tanks and environmental \ninjustic