 {
  "title": "Effect of external and internal loading on source-sink phosphorus dynamics of river sediment amended with iron-rich glauconite sand",
  "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jenvman.2023.117396",
  "source": "Journal of Environmental Management",
  "journal": "Journal of Environmental Management",
  "journal_tier": "top",
  "date": "2023-04-01",
  "category": "basin_eng",
  "department": "其他",
  "region": "国际",
  "quality": "C",
  "summary": "Effect of external and internal loading on source-sink phosphorus dynamics of river sediment amended with iron-rich glauconite sand",
  "tags": [],
  "content_fetched": true,
  "pdf": null,
  "cid": "529e2d115c6f78ec",
  "importance": 5.59,
  "added_at": "2026-10-06",
  "_ev": "ti:44a88237bb77f4eb",
  "quality_src": "B",
  "water_rel": 0.3,
  "kg_terms": [],
  "content_type": "研究文献",
  "kclass": "research",
  "content_class": "academic",
  "gate_status": "keep",
  "gate_reason": "学术文献（top：Journal of Environmental Management）",
  "content": "Effect of external and internal loading on source-sink phosphorus dynamics of river sediment amended with iron-rich glauconite sand \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n -->\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Helpdesk & Helpdocs \n \n \n For professionals \n \n \n News \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n search \n \n \n -->\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Download PDF \n \n \n \n \n \n Journal Of Environmental Management\n \n \n Publication date:\n 2023-04-15 \n \n \n Volume:\n 332\n \n \n \n ISSN:\n 0301-4797 \n \n \n DOI:\n 10.1016/j.jenvman.2023.117396 \n \n \n \n Publisher:\n Elsevier \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Effect of external and internal loading on source-sink phosphorus dynamics of river sediment amended with iron-rich glauconite sand \n \n \n \n Author: \n \n \n \n Xia, Lei \n \n \n \n Verbeeck, Mieke ; Bergen, Benoit ; Smolders, Erik \n \n \n \n \n Keywords: \n \n \n Science & Technology, Life Sciences & Biomedicine, Environmental Sciences, Environmental Sciences & Ecology, Phosphorus dynamics, Fe-rich glauconite sand, Hydrodynamic disturbance, Static incubation, Sediment, WATER TREATMENT RESIDUALS, BIOAVAILABLE PHOSPHORUS, LAKE SEDIMENT, IMMOBILIZATION, LOSSES, ZEOLITE, RELEASE, QUALITY, Phosphorus, Iron, Sand, Rivers, Geologic Sediments, Minerals, Water, Water Pollutants, Chemical, Lakes\n \n \n \n \n Abstract: \n \n Glauconite sands (GS) are abundantly available iron (Fe)-rich minerals that are efficient in lowering the release of phosphorus (P) from sediments to the overlying water. Many river sediments are, however, net sinks for P rather than sources and it is unclear if these GS minerals also enhance the P uptake from water. This is because the concentration of Fe(III) minerals at the sediment-water interface (SWI) depends on the redox potential that is affected by physicochemical processes. This study was set-up to investigate if a sediment amendment with GS can both lower P release from the sediment and enhance P uptake from the overlying water. The P fluxes across the SWI were compared between GS-amended (added at 10% weight fraction) and non-amended river sediment in static (incubation) and dynamic (flume) systems. The net P uptake was measured in response to a pulse external P loading (0.5-5 mg P L-1). Sodium glutamate was added to all treatments to simulate water with a high oxygen demand. Before the P pulse, the GS-amended sediments released significantly less P to the overlying water than the non-amended sediments in both static as dynamic systems. Spiking the water reverted the net P flux over the SWI only in the dynamic system, and the net P uptake in the sediment was factor two larger in GS-amended sediment compared to the non-amended sediment. This study showed that GS addition not only reduced internal P release, but also enhanced P uptake from the overlying water. However, the long-term efficiency in streams likely decreases over time due to saturation processes.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Comments on this page: \n LIBIS \n \n \n Last update: April 8, 2024 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n About us \n \n \n Our mission \n \n \n Our team \n \n \n Our history \n \n \n Our partners \n \n \n KU Leuven \n \n \n KU Leuven Libraries \n \n \n \n \n Our services \n \n \n Collections & Data \n \n \n Services & Tools \n \n \n Expertise & Consultancy \n \n \n Research infrastructure \n \n \n Library \n \n \n Archive \n \n \n Heritage \n \n \n \n \n Our solutions \n \n \n Limo \n \n \n Lirias \n \n \n RDR \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n About Us \n \n Our mission \n Our team \n Our history \n Our partners \n \n \n \n KU Leuven \n KU Leuven Libraries \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Our services \n \n Collections & Data \n Services & Tools \n Expertise &\n Consultancy \n Research\n infrastructure \n \n \n \n Library \n Archive \n Heritage \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Our solutions \n \n Limo \n Lirias \n RDR",
  "content_kind": "fulltext",
  "fulltext_status": "已获取全文",
  "fulltext_source": "Unpaywall(HTML)",
  "fulltext_chars": 3663,
  "fulltext_tried_at": "2026-10-11"
 },
