\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Abstract \n The authors regret that the printed version of the above article contained erroneous units of the bacterial production (BP). The correct and final version follows. The authors would like to apologize for any inconvenience caused. The correct BP data can also be found in Spilling et al. (2022).[Formula presented] Corrigendum to the results paragraph presenting bacterial production. Bacterial production (BP) was elevated in all the treatments with additions (Hum, Nutr and Nutr+Hum) compared with the Contr (Fig. 7; Tukey, p < 0.003). The BP was relatively constant in the treatments with additions throughout the experiment with a mean of 1.13 μmol C L\n −1 d\n −1 . In the Contr, the average BP was 0.74 μmol C L\n −1 d\n −1 . \n Original language English Volume 871 DOIs https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2023.162040 Publication status Published - 2023 Externally published Yes MoE publication type O2 Other Publication series Name Science of the Total Environment Publisher Elsevier ISSN (Print) 0048-9697 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Access to Document \n 10.1016/j.scitotenv.2023.162040 Corrigendum to “Brownification affects phytoplankton community Final published version, 246 KB https://urn.fi/URN:NBN:fi-fe20231006138968 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Fingerprint \n \n \n Dive into the research topics of 'Corrigendum to “Brownification affects phytoplankton community composition but not primary productivity in eutrophic coastal waters: A mesocosm experiment in the Baltic Sea” [Sci. Total Environ. 841 (2022): 156510] (Science of the Total Environment (2022) 841, (S0048969722036075), (10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.156510))'. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Coastal Waters \n Keyphrases \n 100% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Mesocosm Experiment \n Keyphrases \n 100% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Total Environment \n Keyphrases \n 100% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Primary Productivity \n Keyphrase