10] (Science of the Total Environment (2022) 841, (S0048969722036075), (10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.156510)). / Spilling, K.; Asmala, E.; Haavisto, N. et al. 2023. (Science of the Total Environment). Research output : Other contribution › peer-review \n \n \n \n TY - GEN T1 - Corrigendum to “Brownification affects phytoplankton community composition but not primary productivity in eutrophic coastal waters: A mesocosm experiment in the Baltic Sea” [Sci. Total Environ. 841 (2022): 156510] (Science of the Total Environment (2022) 841, (S0048969722036075), (10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.156510)) AU - Spilling, K. AU - Asmala, E. AU - Haavisto, N. AU - Haraguchi, L. AU - Kraft, K. AU - Lehto, A.-M. AU - Lewandowska, A. AU - Norkko, J. AU - Piiparinen, J. AU - Seppälä, J. AU - Vanharanta, M. AU - Vehmaa, A. AU - Ylöstalo, P. AU - Tamminen, T. PY - 2023 Y1 - 2023 N2 - The authors regret that the printed version of the above article contained erroneous units of the bacterial production (BP). The correct and final version follows. The authors would like to apologize for any inconvenience caused. The correct BP data can also be found in Spilling et al. (2022).[Formula presented] Corrigendum to the results paragraph presenting bacterial production. Bacterial production (BP) was elevated in all the treatments with additions (Hum, Nutr and Nutr+Hum) compared with the Contr (Fig. 7; Tukey, p < 0.003). The BP was relatively constant in the treatments with additions throughout the experiment with a mean of 1.13 μmol C L\n −1 d\n −1. In the Contr, the average BP was 0.74 μmol C L\n −1 d\n −1. AB - The authors regret that the printed version of the above article contained erroneous units of the bacterial production (BP). The correct and final version follows. The authors would like to apologize for any inconvenience caused. The correct BP data can also be found in Spilling et al. (2022).[Formula presented] Corrigendum to the results paragraph presenting bacterial production. Bacterial production (BP) was elevated in all the treatments with additions (Hum, Nutr and Nutr+Hum) compared with the Contr (Fig. 7; Tukey, p < 0.003). The BP was relatively constant in the treatments with additions throughout the experiment with a mean of 1.13 μmol C L\n −1 d\n −1. In the Contr, the average BP was 0.74 μmol C L\n −1 d\n −1. U2 - 10.1016/j.scitotenv.2023.162040 DO - 10.1016/j.scitotenv.2023.162040 M3 - Other contribution VL - 871 T3 - Science of the Total Environment ER - \n \n \n \n Spilling K, Asmala E, Haavisto N, Haraguchi L, Kraft K, Lehto AM et al. Corrigendum to “Brownification affects phytoplankton community composition but not primary productivity in eutrophic coastal waters: A mesocosm experiment in the Baltic Sea” [Sci. Total Environ. 841 (2022): 156510] (Science of the Total Environment (2022) 841, (S0048969722036075), (10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.156510)) . 2023. doi: 10.1016/j.scitotenv.2023.162040 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Powered by Pure Link opens in a new tab , Scopus Link opens in a new tab & Elsevier Fingerprint Engine&trade; Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n All content on this site: Copyright &copy; 2026 Åbo Akademi University, its licensors, and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. For all open access content, the relevant licensing terms apply\n \n We use cookies to help provide and enhance our service and tailor content. By continuing you agree to the use of cookies \n \n \n Log in to Pure Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n \n \n \n Åbo Akademi University data protection policy Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n \n About web accessibility Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Report vulnerability Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Contact us",
