 {
  "title": "Causes and impacts of a mine water spill from an acidic pit lake (Iberian Pyrite Belt)",
  "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envpol.2019.04.011",
  "source": "Environmental Pollution",
  "journal": "Environmental Pollution",
  "journal_tier": "top",
  "date": "2019-07-01",
  "category": "basin_eng",
  "department": "其他",
  "region": "国际",
  "quality": "C",
  "summary": "Causes and impacts of a mine water spill from an acidic pit lake (Iberian Pyrite Belt)",
  "tags": [],
  "content_fetched": true,
  "pdf": null,
  "cid": "988fef143b9be03e",
  "importance": 5.59,
  "added_at": "2026-10-08",
  "_ev": "ti:8dc1f0a6151d3a37",
  "quality_src": "B",
  "water_rel": 0.3,
  "kg_terms": [],
  "content_type": "研究文献",
  "kclass": "research",
  "content_class": "academic",
  "gate_status": "keep",
  "gate_reason": "学术文献（top：Environmental Pollution）",
  "content": "Causes and impacts of a mine water spill from an acidic pit lake (Iberian Pyrite Belt) \n \n \n \n \n Skip to main content\n Communities All of Arias Montano Statistics About Arias Montano Español English Français Português Log In My UHU account\n Password login Log in New user? Click here to register. Have you forgotten your password? Home Investigación Artículos Causes and impacts of a mine water spill from an acidic pit lake (Iberian Pyrite Belt) Causes and impacts of a mine water spill from an acidic pit lake (Iberian Pyrite Belt) Loading... Files La Zarza spill_ENV POL clean version_v2.pdf (5.92 MB) Publication date 2019-04-07 Authors Olías Álvarez, Manuel Ruiz Cánovas, Carlos Basallote Sánchez, María Dolores Macías Suárez, Francisco Pérez López, Rafael Moreno González, Raúl Millán Becerro, Ricardo Nieto Liñán, José Miguel Millán Becerro, Ricardo Advisors Department Ciencias de la Tierra Research group Center Related publication Metrics Export Research Projects Organizational Units Journal Issue URI https://hdl.handle.net/10272/22785 DOI doi.org/10.1016/j.envpol.2019.04.011 Abstract In May 2017, a spill from La Zarza pit lake (SW Spain) resulted in the release of approximately 270,000 m3 of extremely acidic waters to the Odiel River. Around 780.000 kg of Fe, 170.000 kg of Al, 2,150 kg of As and high amounts of other trace metals and metalloids were spilled. The purpose of this study is to explain the causes, consequences and impacts of the mine spill on the receiving water bodies. To this end, an extensive sampling along the mine site, river and estuary as well as a hydrological model of the pit lake was performed. Around 53 km of the Odiel River's main course, which was already contaminated by acid mine drainage (AMD), were affected. The mine spill resulted in an incremental impact on the Odiel River water quality. Thus, dissolved concentrations of some elements increased in the river up to 450 times; e.g. 435 mg/L of Fe and 0.41 mg/L of As. Due to low pH values (around 2.5), most metals (e.g., Cu, Zn, Mn, Cd) were transported in the dissolved phase to the estuary, exhibiting a conservative behavior and decreasing their concentration only due to dilution. However, dissolved concentrations of Fe, Cr, Pb, Se, Sb, Ti, V and especially As decreased significantly along the river due to Fe precipitation and sorption/coprecipitation processes. At the upper zone of the estuary, a noticeable increment of metal concentrations (up to 77 times) was also recorded. The water balance illustrates the existence of groundwater inputs (at least 16% of total) to the pit lake, due probably to local infiltration of rainwater at the mining zone. The probable existence of an ancient adit connected to the pit lake indicates that potential releases could occur again if adequate prevention measures are not adopted. Keywords La Zarza ; Acid mine drainage ; Water pollution ; Iberian Pyrite Belt Unesco Subjects 2506.04 Geología Ambiental 2508.11 Calidad de las Aguas 2508.14 Aguas Superficiales Bibliographic citation Environmental Pollution vol. 250 pp: 127-136 doi.org/10.1016/j.envpol.2019.04.011 Collections Artículos Full item page The license for this item is described as Atribución-NoComercial-SinDerivadas 3.0 España The metadata of Arias Montano is subject to: Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal Licenses. Copyright © 2026. ARIAS MONTANO. Repositorio Institucional de la Universidad de Huelva Contact Feedback Cookie settings Privacy Policy",
  "content_kind": "fulltext",
  "fulltext_status": "已获取全文",
  "fulltext_source": "Unpaywall(HTML)",
  "fulltext_chars": 3473,
  "fulltext_tried_at": "2026-10-11"
 },
